text:
The plate holds a single piece of corn on the cob, cut as a short round segment about 100 px across on a plate roughly 350 px wide. If the plate is about 24 cm, the segment is about 7 cm across and 2-3 cm thick. That is a small cob slice.

For mass, a cob slice about 3 cm long and 5 cm across would be roughly 50 g of kernels plus cob. A whole medium ear (about 90 g of kernels) is about 90 kcal. Corn on the cob is about 96 kcal per 100 g edible portion, so a 60 g slice is about 55 kcal.

